{"subjectId":"python","id":"control-flow","title":"Control Flow","group":"Getting Started","order":6,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>if</code>/<code>elif</code>/<code>else</code>, <code>for</code>, <code>while</code>, <code>match</code> — plus a few Python-only twists like <code>for … else</code>.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-git-branch\"></i>Conditionals</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def grade(score):\n    if score &gt;= 90:\n        return \"A\"\n    elif score &gt;= 75:\n        return \"B\"\n    else:\n        return \"C\"\n\nprint(grade(95), grade(80), grade(40))       # A B C\nstatus = \"adult\" if 20 &gt;= 18 else \"minor\"     # conditional expression\nprint(status)                                  # adult</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-repeat\"></i>Loops</h3>\n<p><code>for</code> iterates over <em>any iterable</em> (lists, strings, dicts, files, generators). <code>while</code> repeats while a condition is truthy.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>for i in range(2, 10, 3):          # start, stop (exclusive), step\n    print(i, end=\" \")               # 2 5 8\nprint()\nfor i, ch in enumerate(\"abc\", start=1):\n    print(i, ch, end=\" | \")         # 1 a | 2 b | 3 c |\nprint()\nfor name, age in zip([\"a\", \"b\"], [20, 30]):\n    print(name, age, end=\"; \")      # a 20; b 30;</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Helper</th><th>Gives you</th><th>Instead of</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>enumerate(it)</code></td><td><code>(index, item)</code> pairs</td><td><code>for i in range(len(xs))</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>zip(a, b)</code></td><td>Items side by side (stops at the shortest)</td><td>Manual index juggling</td></tr><tr><td><code>reversed(seq)</code></td><td>Items back to front, lazily</td><td><code>seq[::-1]</code> (copies)</td></tr><tr><td><code>sorted(it, key=…)</code></td><td>A new sorted list</td><td>Sorting then copying</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>More patterns — <code>while … else</code>, breaking out of nested loops, sentinel loops, modifying while iterating — are in <strong>Loops &amp; Iteration Patterns</strong>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-player-skip-forward\"></i><code>break</code>, <code>continue</code> and loop <code>else</code></h3>\n<p>A loop's <code>else</code> block runs only if the loop finished <strong>without</strong> <code>break</code> — perfect for search loops.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def find_first_negative(nums):\n    for i, n in enumerate(nums):\n        if n &lt; 0:\n            break\n    else:\n        return None          # no break → nothing found\n    return i\n\nprint(find_first_negative([3, 1, -2, 5]))   # 2\nprint(find_first_negative([1, 2]))          # None</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-binary-tree\"></i><code>match</code> — structural pattern matching (3.10+)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def describe(cmd):\n    match cmd:\n        case [\"go\", direction]:\n            return f\"moving {direction}\"\n        case [\"pick\", *items] if items:\n            return f\"picking {len(items)} items\"\n        case {\"action\": \"quit\"}:\n            return \"bye\"\n        case int() | float() as n:\n            return f\"number {n}\"\n        case _:\n            return \"unknown\"\n\nprint(describe([\"go\", \"north\"]))       # moving north\nprint(describe([\"pick\", \"a\", \"b\"]))    # picking 2 items\nprint(describe({\"action\": \"quit\"}))    # bye\nprint(describe(3.5))                   # number 3.5</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>match</code> is not a C <code>switch</code>: it destructures sequences, mappings and objects, binds names, and supports guards (<code>if</code>). See <strong>Pattern Matching (match)</strong> for every pattern kind and its pitfalls.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>No <code>do … while</code>, no <code>++</code></h3>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"callout callout--good\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Do</div><p>Use <code>while True:</code> with a <code>break</code> at the end for do-while logic, and <code>i += 1</code> to increment.</p></div><div class=\"callout callout--bad\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Avoid</div><p>Writing <code>i++</code> (a syntax error) or <code>++i</code> (parsed as <code>+(+i)</code> — silently does nothing).</p></div></div></section>"}